Subject: [PATCH 0055] Visualizar > Tamanho da Interface (Automático / 100 / 125 / 150 %)

A 1x Mac screen draws a 24 dp icon in 24 px with 2 px strokes, so curves and
diagonals look stepped next to a phone. The menu writes the choice to
<android-root>/.macapk/ui_scale ("auto" = the largest size whose phone window fits
the screen); the host launcher turns it into the display density and scaled
window sizes, so the app still sees a 412 dp phone (or 1280 dp tablet) drawn with
more pixels. Density is fixed per process, as on Android: a change reopens the app.

